# Extra LAN addresses on eth0, one per line, read by
# /usr/local/sbin/homelab-extra-addresses.
#
# These came across with the stacks from the old moby (192.168.1.25), which
# held .72-.78 as secondary addresses on one NIC and published each stack's
# ports on its own address. The compose files bind those addresses by name, so
# the addresses moved with them rather than every stack being rewritten.
#
# They sit in the range ../CLAUDE.md pencils in for Non-Production while this
# container is pooled Infrastructure. That is inherited, not a new convention -
# see moby/CLAUDE.md.
#
# pct only carries one address per interface, and Proxmox rewrites
# /etc/network/interfaces in the container on every start, so this cannot live
# in either. Adding an address here needs a DNS record too (dns/).
192.168.1.73    # nextcloud: web publishes :80 and :443
192.168.1.74    # traefik: publishes :80, :443 and the :8080 dashboard
192.168.1.79    # home assistant: nginx serves it on :443, app binds loopback
